You need domain knowledge, e.g., PDEs and Navier-Stokes equations, to check whether a formal definition matches its intended informal counterpart. Right of the bat, the latter is interpreted in the ZFC axiomatic system. Here, humans do math with mathematical interpretation or semantics. Down to the kernel level, on the other hand, everything in Lean is either term or type as a dependent type theory, which merely reflects syntax. So, there are at least two potential mismatches: types vs sets, semantics vs syntax.

